{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` has two obligations. The first is that each bundled skill opens with its workflow, before any other section. The second is that the workflow is ordered steps. The requirement is distributed, so each skill's own review covers whether it upholds these. The test covers the requirement itself.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]` loops over `SKILLS`, which lists all five bundled skills. For each skill it checks three things:\n- The first `## ` heading in `SKILL.md` equals `## Workflow`. This enforces that the workflow is the first section.\n- `workflow_steps` yields at least two steps. The helper finds `- [ ] N. text` items in the Workflow section and stops at the next `## `.\n- The step numbers equal `1..=n`, so the steps are numbered and in order.\n\nThe test would fail if a skill put another `##` section first, had no numbered steps, or had steps out of order or with gaps. It is also marked with `{test}`.\n\n**Site query `skills`.** `run_named_query` returned exactly the five `assets/skills/*/SKILL.md` files, which are the five skills the test iterates over. A text search of `assets/skills` for headings found no other front-matter skill files. The reference `.md` files under `references/` begin with an h1 and no front matter, so the query rightly excludes them. The match snippet has front matter. The no_match snippet has none, so the two snippets show the distinction the query relies on.\n\n**Result.** I found no gap in the test, the site query, or the obligations.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
